Monkeys Typing

This repository contains a local command-line Python app inspired by the infinite monkey theorem.

At startup the program shows the title "(Not quite infinite monkeys (only 1 actually) Typing)." and a short description, then asks how many characters the monkey should type.

The character count range is 100 to 1,000,000,000.

It also asks which character set to use:

1. Lowercase letters and spaces
2. Uppercase letters and spaces
3. Uppercase and lowercase letters and spaces
4. All characters

Then it asks which run mode to use:

1. Display generated characters in terminal
2. Fast mode (no character rendering)
3. Fast mode with output file

Large runs are processed in batches of 10,000 with progress and ETA updates.

For very long runs, the app can save checkpoints and resume later from the last saved batch.

The result review only shows likely real English words and phrases, or nothing at all if none are found.

Run it with:

```powershell
python -m monkeys_typing
```

The project uses a `src/` layout and is set up for git-based development with the GitHub remote already configured.
